#### Undoing instruction changes made in the lens

If you need to revert changes made in the lens, you can do so directly from the step file in VS Code—provided the VS Code session is still open.

1. Open the step file

2. The step file opens to the side. *- red rectangle*

3. With the step file focused, type `Ctrl+Z` to roll back the last edit made in the lens instructions. *- yellow rectangle*

{{::il.DA_EditStepFile_Undo_img}}

